---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Claim from '../../components/Claim.astro';
import ResultsTable from '../../components/ResultsTable.astro';
import Fig from '../../components/Fig.astro';
import Tex from '../../components/Tex.astro';
import FringeHero from '../../components/figures/FringeHero.astro';
import BellTable from '../../components/figures/BellTable.astro';
import DensityMatrix from '../../components/figures/DensityMatrix.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/site';
import setup from '../../assets/figures/bs-setup.png';
import cones from '../../assets/figures/bs-cones.png';
import depol from '../../assets/figures/bs-depolarisation.png';

const src = 'Verma, BS thesis, IISc (2024).';
---

<CaseStudy
  slug="entangled-photon-source"
  setting="Quantum Optics & Quantum Information Lab, Department of Instrumentation and Applied Physics, IISc Bengaluru"
  contribution={[
    {
      text: 'This thesis gave me a working understanding of the entangled-photon source and hands-on experience with it and its measurements. Building the source was not my work alone.',
      basis: 'Author’s statement, October 2026.',
    },
    { text: 'I wrote and submitted the thesis.', basis: 'Thesis declaration, April 2024.' },
  ]}
  collaborators={[
    {
      text: 'C. M. Chandrashekar supervised the thesis. Members of the Quantum Optics and Quantum Information lab are thanked in the acknowledgements; their individual roles are not stated.',
      basis: 'BS thesis, certificate and acknowledgements.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>
      A random number generator is only as trustworthy as the evidence that its output comes from a quantum process.
      This thesis asks how the quality of random bits drawn from entangled photons relates to the quality of the
      entanglement, and how a Bell violation can certify that the data are quantum.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="method">
    <p>
      Photon pairs come from spontaneous parametric down-conversion in a 10 mm type-II PPKTP crystal with quasi-phase
      matching. The down-converted light cones were imaged with an EMCCD camera. Entanglement was checked three ways:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>a Bell–CHSH test from coincidence counts at four pairs of polarizer settings,</li>
      <li>polarization-correlation visibility curves with the first polarizer at H, D, V and A,</li>
      <li>quantum state tomography, giving Stokes parameters, the density matrix and the state fidelity.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The CHSH value combines four correlations, each computed from four coincidence counts:</p>
    <Tex block tex={String.raw`E(a,b)=\frac{N_{ab}+N_{a_\perp b_\perp}-N_{a b_\perp}-N_{a_\perp b}}{N_{ab}+N_{a_\perp b_\perp}+N_{a b_\perp}+N_{a_\perp b}},\qquad S=\bigl|E(a,b)-E(a,b')+E(a',b)+E(a',b')\bigr|`} />
    <p>
      Random bits come from measuring the polarization of one photon. The thesis tests them with the NIST suite, splits
      them into odd and even bits, applies Toeplitz and XOR extractors, and studies how depolarization with a half-wave
      plate lowers both S and the randomness.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="results">
    <p>
      The thesis reports <Claim id="bs.chsh" /> from the Table 5.1 counts, above the local bound of 2, a state fidelity
      of <Claim id="bs.fidelity" /> from tomography, and a bit rate of <Claim id="bs.rate" /> at 6 mW pump power, with
      the bits passing <Claim id="bs.nist" bare /> NIST tests without post-processing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The four-qubit QRNG paper reports its own characterisation of the source it used. Those numbers are on{' '}
      <a href={url('/research/four-qubit-qrng/')}>that case study</a> and are not combined with the thesis values here.
    </p>
    <ResultsTable ids={['bs.chsh', 'bs.fidelity', 'bs.rate', 'bs.nist']} />
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="interactive">
    <h3>Visibility curves</h3>
    <FringeHero />
    <h3>The Bell test, from the raw counts</h3>
    <p>Pick one of the four correlation terms to see which counts it uses.</p>
    <BellTable />
    <h3>Reconstructed state</h3>
    <DensityMatrix />
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="figures">
    <Fig src={setup} alt="Schematic of the polarization-entangled photon setup with pump, crystal and two detection arms." caption="Figure 5.1. Experimental setup." source={src} />
    <Fig src={cones} alt="EMCCD images of SPDC light cones for horizontal, vertical and both polarizations." caption="Figure 5.2. SPDC light cones imaged on an EMCCD camera at the degenerate temperature with an 810 nm bandpass filter." source={src} />
    <Fig src={depol} alt="Line plot of S value falling from about 2.7 towards zero as the half-wave-plate angle increases to about 24 degrees." caption="Figure 5.6. Effect of depolarization on the S value as a function of half-wave-plate angle." source={src} />
  </Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
